{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":82175,"duration_api_ms":185639,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e728d454-e6c6-4bdd-af2a-e55ca4592bf0","total_cost_usd":0.5771145499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30884,"cache_read_input_tokens":87864,"output_tokens":2747,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30884,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":319,"outputTokens":11856,"cacheReadInputTokens":1110248,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80671,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27146255,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2747,"cacheReadInputTokens":87864,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30884,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.305652,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all five amendments against current source. The two documentation/maintainability amendments (fr-3-df697556, fr-3-77143f76) identify real inconsistencies in the code. The three defect claims (fr-3-dc32db9e, fr-3-3d1fd76b, fr-3-bc5a66d7) describe bugs that are not present in the current implementation — the code already handles depth in substrate area derivation, uses water_depth_above_substrate_cm() for light calculations, and recomputes crowding from live biomass on every registry refresh.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-df697556","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: compute_habitat_registry() builds HabitatEnv.light_intensity from hardware.light.intensity_index only (habitat.rs:105-109). It never reads photoperiod_hours. ChangePhotoperiod in affects_habitat_registry() therefore triggers a redundant registry refresh. The mismatch is real and should be tightened or documented."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-77143f76","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: total_colonizable_area_cm2() (biology.rs:660-669) sums wall_area_cm2 + substrate layer areas, omitting geometry.hardscape_area_cm2. Meanwhile compute_glass_hardscape() (habitat.rs:172) includes both wall + hardscape in the habitat registry. The algae carrying-capacity model in algae_growth.rs:173-175 uses the legacy helper and therefore ignores hardscape surfaces. A TODO or doc comment clarifying this gap for the downstream habitatization task is justified."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-dc32db9e","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified: SubstrateLayerState::derived_colonizable_area_cm2() (substrate.rs:54-58) computes footprint_area_cm2 * depth_cm * colonizable_area_factor — depth IS included. refresh_habitat_registry() (state.rs:258-270) rewrites each layer's colonizable_area_cm2 from this derivation, and compute_substrate_deep() (habitat.rs:222-228) sums freshly derived values. Scenario materialization also calls the depth-aware derivation. The claimed geometry-insensitive behavior is not present in the current code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-3d1fd76b","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified: habitat.rs:94-95 computes substrate light using state.water_depth_above_substrate_cm(), not geometry.mean_depth_cm(). The water_depth_above_substrate_cm() method (state.rs:200-203) subtracts substrate_depth_cm from fill_height_cm, so a deeper substrate bed correctly results in less water above it and more light reaching the substrate surface. The bug described — that substrate thickness is ignored — is not present."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bc5a66d7","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified: refresh_habitat_registry() (state.rs:258-262) calls derived_plant_crowding_index() which recomputes crowding from current live biomass_g values (state.rs:223-230), then writes the result back to all plant guilds before recomputing the registry. Both trim actions are marked as habitat-affecting (actions.rs:162-163), so the engine calls refresh_habitat_registry() immediately after reducing biomass. Crowding is therefore updated from post-trim biomass, not stale."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"531f68f6-a27d-4374-8a49-2f5910240579"}
